  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a plan, but I haven't changed any code, because plan mode is still on. I couldn't submit the plan for approval either: the plan-approval tool is disabled in this session. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir`. `convert` passes `dir=1` for the minimum and `dir=-1` for the maximum. So with an open bound, a value below the minimum clamps to `min-1` and a value above the maximum clamps to `max+1`. Both are outside the allowed range.\n\n**Fix:** change that line to `return bound + dir`. An open minimum then clamps to `min+1` and an open maximum to `max-1`.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add two cases to `test_range` in `tests/test_types.py`:\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `\"-5\"` should return 1.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `\"9\"` should return 4.\n\nThen I'd run `pytest tests/test_types.py -k range` and the full suite.\n\n**Not touched:** I'd leave these edge cases alone unless you want them handled:\n- `min > max`.\n- Open bounds with no valid integer between them.\n- NaN in `FloatRange`.\n- `inf` in `IntRange`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-snuggly-sunset.md`.",
